# AI_CONTEXT continuity (QuantLab)

```text
DERIVED_CONTEXT=YES
CANONICAL_AUTHORITY=NO
Repo > docs/governance/** > AI_CONTEXT/ > chat
```

## Bootstrap

New / cold sessions: read `AI_CONTEXT/BOOTSTRAP.md` first, then `PROJECT_STATE.md` + the agent handoff. Do not reconstruct project truth from chat history.

## When to update AI_CONTEXT

Only on **material** change:

- phase / gate / Owner Gate
- P0/P1 open or close
- capability, feature flag, runtime, or deploy truth
- architecture decision or significant HOLD
- important failure / RCA
- formal iteration closure

At formal iteration end: **check** whether `PROJECT_STATE`, `LAST_ITERATIONS`, `CHATGPT_HANDOFF`, `CURSOR_HANDOFF` need refresh.

## When not to update

Trivial edits, cosmetic commits, log dumps, or timestamp-only bumps.

## Hard forbids

- Chat transcripts / chain-of-thought in AI_CONTEXT
- Copying Constitution, Ledgers, or full governance bodies into AI_CONTEXT
- Creating a parallel SSOT under `AI_CONTEXT/`
- Letting stale handoff override code, runtime, or `docs/governance/**`

On conflict: fix AI_CONTEXT; never “fix” canonical truth from derived memory.

Indexes (`DECISION_INDEX`, `FAILURE_INDEX`, `CAPABILITY_INDEX`) stay **link-only**.
